To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:Help with tcpd?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078614710593

Thanks to Gyula Szokoly, Stephen LaBelle, Dan Riley, and Mika Tuupola for
prompt replies to my query about building tcp wrappers and using the
"spawn (logging to an external file)" format in my hosts.allow and hosts.deny.

The way to do this is to be sure to uncomment the line:

STYLE	= -DPROCESS_OPTIONS	# Enable language extensions

in the Makefile. "-DPROCESS_OPTIONS" can also be included in the command
line - I had done that before, and that's what confused me, because it
leaves no record in the Makefile of what you did for future reference.

Thanks again!!

-- 
Judith Reed
jreed@appliedtheory.com

