To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] VXT2000 won't boot
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078614710548

Dear Gurus,

Since I installed DU4.0B my VXT2000s refuse to boot through joind.

I finally managed to install an Infoserver, which solves the problem.

However, I still don't know why this happened. I include the answers
from John F. Marten and Michael Matthews. I could not test if things
would have gone better after having installed the obsolete bootpd.

Thanks!

Jean-Loup

------------
John's answer:

i have a application that needs bootpd. copy the line in your inetd.conf
that has bootps(joind), then comment one of them out. then replace joind with 
bootpd :
bootps	dgram udp wait root  /usr/sbin/bootpd  bootpd

now, copy /usr/opt/obsolete/usr/sbin/bootpd to /usr/sbin

then make the appropriate entry in bootptab including a bf= for an extended 
bootfile if applicable.
------------
Michael's answer:

bootpd isn't in /usr/sbin any more.  It's in the obsolete set:

OSFOBSOLETE410.inv:0    65536   32863   3       4       100755  11/15/96
410     f       ./usr/opt/obsolete/usr/sbin/bootpd      none   
OSFOBSOLETE410

