Subject: SUMMARY: Maximum # of users allowed by OSF-USR license PAK
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078614710440


(Original question appended below)

Thanks to the following gurus for helping me solve the problem:

Bjorn S. Nilsson,
Andreas Lundgren,
Sheryl A. Campbell,
Groeten, Alex Kok,
Jorge Granjal, 
Richard Eisenman,
Sher,
Mike Hannon.

As many pointed out, the maxusers parameter has nothing to do with
the actual number of users that is allowed to log in. That is determined
by the licenses. When I upgraded the system, a temporary license was
installed.

The solution was to use the License Management Facility (lmf) to register
the PAK's from the DEC Campus CD-ROM, and delete the temporary and the old
ones. The process was:

* copy the paks from the CD to /paks_unix
* register the new PAK:          # lmf register - < /paks_unix/osf-usr
* list PAK's registered:         # lmf list full for OSF-USR
* remove the old registrations:  # lmf delete OSF-USR DEC authorization
  where authorization is the Authorization Number
* update the license in kernel:  # lmf load 0 USR-OSF

I now have:
# lmf list | grep OSF-USR
OSF-USR                   active                            unlimited

Lesson learned: remember to register the system after an upgrade.

