Date: Mon, 14 Jul 1997 13:23:48 -0500 (CDT)
From: Tim Mooney <mooney@dogbert.cc.ndsu.NoDak.edu>
To: "Paul N. Youngblood" <youngbp@email.uah.edu>
Subject: Re: SUMMARY: dxaccounts quit creating quota for new users

Paul-

Sorry for the late reply, but I thought I would check with you on this.
By any chance, are you re-using uids?  I mean are you purging users and
then re-assigning their uid to some new login?  That would explain why
you're seeing this phenomenon, since the quota.{user,group} files don't get
cleaned out when you purge a user unless you explicitly set the user's
quotas to 0 on all filesystems before you actually delete them from the
system.

Tim
