From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Jul 07 19:21:06 1997
From: "R. Lee Hawkins" <lhawkins () annie ! wellesley ! edu>
Date: Mon, 07 Jul 1997 19:21:06 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: maxuprc and physmem under OSF/DU
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078614710256



First, thanks to:

matthewm@voyager.sgate.com (Michael Matthews)
and
alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com

Michael and Alan both pointed out that physmem is not needed in OSF/DU.
Michael pointed out the dxkerneltuner command, which revealed that

data-limit-per-proc

was set to 128Mb.  We've upped that to 3*128Mb, which should take care
of the problem.   This command also allows direct tuning of many other
kernel params, including maxuprc.

And yes, we really do need to create arrays larger than 128Mb (for image
analysis).

Cheers,
