-  	In the past we've received the "dquot: table full" message 
	in the messages file. After running quotacheck -v a few times
	the message would go away. A more permanent solution was to
	move the maxusers value in the kernel to 64.  Since this time
	this error has no shown up again.

-       But the problem has surfaced again.  This time random users
	were unable to create files do to an exceed quota.  But 
        when we checked their quota they we just fine (ie not close
	to exceeding it).  Various quotacheck -v reported errors but
	did nothing to fix the problem.  Rebooting and doing quotacheck -v
	did nothing to fix the problem.  Finally, we just turned quota's
        off and went home for the night.  When we returned and turned
	quota's back on, everything worked fine.


Question:
