> tack@dstu.univ-montp2.fr



Josiane,

that is how we drive most of our decstations since about 2 years.
(Diskless and Ultrix 4.3)

If i remember right, the only thing you need to do is to modify
/etc/rc.local a bit.

Following is the end of a rc.local of an ultrix-machine, which
comes up with the CDE-chooser after a reboot.

###  Begin of extract  ###

# starting the chooser from machine abc.full.qualified.hostname
echo 'Starting Xws with special CHOOSER'                        >/dev/console
/usr/bin/Xws bc -indirect abc.full.qualified.hostname \
        > /var/adm/X0msgs 2>> /var/adm/X0msgs < /dev/null &
#
# to start xdm on this ultrix-machine,
# which seems to be necessary for CHOOSER
#
[ -f /usr/bin/X11/xdm ] && {
        /usr/bin/X11/xdm & echo -n ' xdm started' > /dev/console
}

###  End of extract  ###


The only other thing is to have an appropriate xdm-setup
on machine abc.full.qualified.hostname.

In our case this a du-4.0a alphastation and the setup-file
should be  /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xaccess.
The easiest way is a "*" that any machine that requests
"chooser/indirect hosts" can be shown all machines that are
running xdm.

Hope this helps.

