Hello Alpha managers,
 I have a question about increasing swap space.  I have
increased the swap space on my Alpha by adding 1GB on another disk
to the 256MB already existing.  I am doing this because I am going to
upgrade my RAM from 256 MB to 1024MB.  My question is:  Am I right in
thinking that I don't need to rebuild the kernel when increasing swap?  I
have checked swapon -s after rebooting and adding the new swap to
the /etc/fstab and it indicates the new swap exists.  My boss would like
confirmation that a kernel rebuild isn't necessary.  
Thanks,
